```text
Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO
To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Mark Christensen, Planner II
Subject: A Resolution Pursuant to Wyoming Statute § 15-9-107 Finding and Declaring Parts of the
15th Street Corridor in the City of Cheyenne as Blight and Authorizing the Redevelopment
Thereof.
Date:
April 20, 2022

Background:
The item for consideration is a Resolution.

The proposed Governing Body review schedule is as follows:
•
Introduction and Referral

04/25/2022
•
Public Services Committee

05/03/2022
•
Second and final reading

05/09/2022

Summary:

The Governing Body adopted the first Blight Study for the City of Cheyenne on June 28, 2022. The
adoption of this Resolution allowed for the creation of the City of Cheyenne Urban Renewal Authority
and authorized the Hitching Post Urban Renewal Plan and Project. In addition to the Hitching Post, the
original Blight Study authorizes the Reed Avenue Rail Corridor and the Hynds/Hole as other areas in the
community eligible for Urban Renewal Projects. Since the adoption, the City has identified the 15th
Street Corridor as another area within the community that may be eligible for an Urban Renewal Plan
and Project. However; Wyoming Statute § 15-9-107 states that, “An urban renewal project for an urban
renewal area shall not be planned or initiated unless the governing body, by resolution, has determined
the area to be a slum area or a blighted area or a combination thereof and designated it as appropriate
for an urban renewal project.” This Resolution and accompanying Blight Study overviews the conditions
of blight found on the 15th Street Corridor and finds that the area outlined in the Study is appropriate for
an Urban Renewal Project, thus satisfying Wyoming Statute § 15-9-107 for the W. 15th Street Corridor.

Attachments:
1. Resolution
2. Exhibit A: Conditions of Blight

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
